IMPORT `cp6-provinces-and-consent`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 113.1 -- THE FINANCIAL REVIEW EVERY THREE YEARS, AND HOW THE CONTRIBUTION RATES MOVE.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2883 to 3013 of the Act file.
--
-- Every three years the Minister of Finance and the ministers of the included provinces review the Plan and may recommend changes
-- to benefits and rates (subsections (1) to (5)). The Governor in Council may then change the rates in Schedules 1 and 2 by regulation
-- (subsection (6)), within limits (7), coming into force on 1 January after the period (8), with provincial consent (8.1).
-- If the rates are found insufficient, Schedule 1 is DEEMED amended without any regulation (subsections (11.05) to (11.14)):
-- the employee and employer rate rises to a rate worked out by one of five formulas, and the self-employed rate becomes twice the employer rate.
-- Subsections (11.141) to (11.146) do the same for the additional Canada Pension Plan by regulations that are not among the texts
-- this encoding reads.
--
-- THE RATE FORMULAS ARE THE COMPUTATION OF THIS MODULE. A, B, C and D are the Act's letters (subsection (11.06)); A and C are halves
-- of the Chief Actuary's rates, B is the rate in force, D is B less C. Rates are fractions: 4.95% is 0.0495.
-- Subsection (11.14) rounds "to the nearest multiple of 0.005%": a rate exactly halfway between two multiples is rounded up (fork C6-F19;
-- the language's own ROUND would round it to the even multiple, which the text does not say).
-- Three-year periods begin in 1998 and every third year after, from "once every three years after 1997" (fork C6-F18).
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS: the ministers' duty to review and the contributor's liability to the rates that follow; the Governor in Council's power
-- to change the rates and the contributor's liability to the new rate, within the immunity the limits of subsection (7) give (no rise of more
-- than 0.1 percentage point a year for employees and employers, 0.2 for the self-employed); the deemed increase of subsections (11.05) to (11.14)
-- (the contributor's liability, with no regulation to wait for); the provinces' consent as a condition on the Governor in Council's power.
--
-- Inert (NOTES.md): subsections (6), (9), (11.144) and (14) (regulation-making powers and an exemption from the Statutory Instruments Act);
-- subsections (11) to (11.04) are repealed in this text. Subsection (12) is written in cp6-provinces-and-consent.l4, beside section 114.

§ `Part III -- the financial review and the movement of the rates (section 113.1)`

§§ `Subsections (1) to (4) -- the review`

-- "Once every three years after 1997": the first period begins in 1998 and each later one three years after it, so a period begins in a
-- year that is a whole number of threes after 1998 (fork C6-F18). NOTHING: the section requires no review before 1998.
-- src:2884 | Financial Review of the Canada Pension Plan
-- src:2885 | Review every three years
-- src:2886 | 113.1 (1) Once every three years after 1997, the Minister of Finance and ministers of the Crown from the included provinces shall review the financial state of the Canada Pension Plan and may make recommendations as to whether benefits, contribution rates, first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates should be changed.
@ref Act s 113.1(1) (src:2884-2886)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 113.1(1) — the first year of the three-year period that contains a year` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 1998
    THEN JUST (year MINUS ((year MINUS 1998) MODULO 3))
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 113.1(1) (src:2884-2886)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(1) — the ministers must review the financial state of the Plan in the three-year period that contains the year` year MEANS
    year AT LEAST 1998

-- src:2887 | Review of adjustment factors
-- src:2888 | (2) When the Chief Actuary of the Office of the Superintendent of Financial Institutions specifies adjustment factors in his or her report according to subsection 115(1.11), the Minister of Finance and ministers of the Crown from the included provinces shall, as part of their review, also review the adjustment factors fixed under subsection 46(7) and may make recommendations as to whether they should be changed.
-- out of range: subsection 46(7) (piece cp3) fixes the adjustment factors; this module only requires the review.
@ref Act s 113.1(2) (src:2887-2888)
GIVEN `the Chief Actuary has specified adjustment factors in the report according to subsection 115(1.11)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(2) — the ministers must as part of their review also review the adjustment factors fixed under subsection 46(7)` `the Chief Actuary has specified adjustment factors in the report according to subsection 115(1.11)` MEANS
    `the Chief Actuary has specified adjustment factors in the report according to subsection 115(1.11)`

-- "before the end of the second year of the three year period": the last day of the second year.
-- src:2889 | Completion of review
-- src:2890 | (3) If possible, the review in each three year period must be completed in time to permit the Minister of Finance to make recommendations to the Governor in Council before the end of the second year of the three year period.
@ref Act s 113.1(3) (src:2889-2890)
GIVEN `the first year of the three-year period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113.1(3) — the end of the second year of the three-year period, before which the Minister of Finance should be able to make recommendations` `the first year of the three-year period` MEANS
    YearMonthDay ((`the first year of the three-year period`) PLUS 1) 12 31

-- src:2891 | Factors to be considered
-- src:2892 | (4) In conducting any review required by this section and in making any recommendations, ministers shall consider
-- src:2893 | (a) the most recent report prepared by the Chief Actuary pursuant to section 115 and any changes between that report and earlier reports prepared by the Chief Actuary;
-- src:2894 | (b) any more recent estimates of the Chief Actuary in respect of
-- src:2895 | (i) the outstanding balance of the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account,
-- src:2896 | (ii) the projected revenues into and payments out of the Canada Pension Plan Account and the Additional Canada Pension Plan Account,
-- src:2897 | (iii) the ratio of the projected assets over the projected expenditures of the base Canada Pension Plan and the additional Canada Pension Plan, and
-- src:2898 | (iv) the changes, if any, to the amounts and ratios projected at the previous review under this section attributable to changing demographic and economic circumstances or to changes to the base Canada Pension Plan or the additional Canada Pension Plan affecting payments or contributions under the Canada Pension Plan;
-- src:2899 | (c) the financing objective, for the base Canada Pension Plan, of having a contribution rate, without taking into account the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph (e) for which the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii) exceeds zero, that is no lower than the rate
-- src:2900 | (i) that, beginning with the year 2003, is the lowest constant rate that can be maintained over the foreseeable future, and
-- src:2901 | (ii) that results in the ratio of the projected assets of the base Canada Pension Plan at the end of any given year over the projected expenditures of the base Canada Pension Plan in the following year being generally constant;
-- src:2902 | (d) the financing objective, for the additional Canada Pension Plan, of having additional contribution rates, without taking into account the changes, if any, referred to in paragraph (e) for which the additional contribution rates most recently calculated under subparagraphs 115(1.1)(d)(ii) and (e)(ii) exceed zero, that are no lower than the rates
-- src:2903 | (i) that, beginning with the year 2024, are the lowest constant rates that can be maintained over the foreseeable future, and
-- src:2904 | (ii) that result in projected contributions and investment income that are sufficient to fully pay the projected expenditures of the additional Canada Pension Plan over the foreseeable future; and
-- src:2905 | (e) that changes to the Act that increase benefits or add new benefits must be accompanied by a permanent increase in the contribution rates under this Act to cover the extra costs of the increased or new benefits and by a temporary increase in the contribution rates under this Act for a number of years that is consistent with common actuarial practice to fully pay any unfunded liability resulting from the increased or new benefits.
@ref Act s 113.1(4) (src:2891-2905)
DECLARE `cp6 Matter in a review under subsection 113.1(4)` IS ONE OF
    `the most recent report of the Chief Actuary under section 115 and changes since earlier reports`
    `more recent estimates of the Chief Actuary of the account balances, projected revenues and payments, projected asset ratios and changes since the previous review`
    `the financing objective for the base Canada Pension Plan`
    `the financing objective for the additional Canada Pension Plan`
    `that changes that increase benefits or add new benefits must be accompanied by contribution rate increases`
    `another matter`

@ref Act s 113.1(4) (src:2891-2905)
GIVEN matter IS A `cp6 Matter in a review under subsection 113.1(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(4) — the ministers must consider the matter` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `another matter` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Subsections (5) to (10) -- recommendations, regulations changing the rates, limits, coming into force`

