    `the recommendations made under subsection 113.1(1) are that no changes be made to benefits, contribution rates, first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates`

-- Subsection (6) (lines 2908 and 2909), the Governor in Council's power to amend Schedule 1 or 2 by regulation, is inert: NOTES.md.

-- (7): "(a) the rates for employees and employers for a year must be identical; (b) the rates for self-employed persons for a year must be
-- equal to the sum of the rates for employees and employers for that year". The same relation is required of the Chief Actuary's rates by
-- section 115(1.2), which calls this rule.
-- src:2910 | Limitation on changes
-- src:2911 | (7) The following shall apply with respect to any changes to and setting of the rates under subsection (6):
-- src:2912 | (a) the rates for employees and employers for a year must be identical;
-- src:2913 | (b) the rates for self-employed persons for a year must be equal to the sum of the rates for employees and employers for that year;
@ref Act s 113.1(7)(a), (b) (src:2910-2913)
GIVEN `the rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(7)(a) and (b) — the rates for the year stand in the required relation` `the rate for employees for the year` `the rate for employers for the year` `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` MEANS
        `the rate for employees for the year` EQUALS `the rate for employers for the year`
    AND `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` EQUALS (`the rate for employees for the year`) PLUS (`the rate for employers for the year`)

-- "(c) no rate for employees and employers for a year may be increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point above the rate for the
-- previous year": an increase of exactly 0.1 percentage point is allowed.
-- src:2914 | (c) no rate for employees and employers for a year may be increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point above the rate for the previous year; and
@ref Act s 113.1(7)(c) (src:2914)
GIVEN `the rate for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(7)(c) — the rate for employees or employers is not increased by more than one-tenth of a percentage point` `the rate for the year` `the rate for the previous year` MEANS
    (`the rate for the year`) MINUS (`the rate for the previous year`) AT MOST 0.1%

-- src:2915 | (d) no rate for self-employed persons for a year may be increased by more than two-tenths of a percentage point above the rate for the previous year.
@ref Act s 113.1(7)(d) (src:2915)
GIVEN `the rate for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(7)(d) — the rate for self-employed persons is not increased by more than two-tenths of a percentage point` `the rate for the year` `the rate for the previous year` MEANS
    (`the rate for the year`) MINUS (`the rate for the previous year`) AT MOST 0.2%

@ref Act s 113.1(7) (src:2910-2915)
GIVEN `the rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for employees for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for employers for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate for self-employed persons for the previous year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
