§§ `Subsections (11.05) to (11.14) -- insufficient rates: the deemed increase`

-- (11.06) A, B, C, D. "A is one half of the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) for self-employed persons
-- for the years in the three-year period"; "C is one half of the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)";
-- "B is the contribution rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which contribution rates
-- were set"; "D is the difference between B and C".
-- src:2931 | Interpretation
-- src:2932 | (11.06) In the calculations under subsections (11.07) to (11.11),
-- src:2933 | A is one half of the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period referred to in subsection (11.05);
-- src:2934 | B is the contribution rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which contribution rates were set for employees and employers, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under subsection (6), on the recommendation of ministers under subsection (1);
-- src:2935 | C is one half of the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii) for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period referred to in subsection (11.05); and
-- src:2936 | D is the difference between B and C.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.06) (src:2931-2936)
GIVEN `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.06) — A` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` MEANS
    (`the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)`) DIVIDED BY 2

@ref Act s 113.1(11.06) (src:2931-2936)
GIVEN `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.06) — C` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` MEANS
    (`the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`) DIVIDED BY 2

@ref Act s 113.1(11.06) (src:2931-2936)
GIVEN `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.06) — D` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` MEANS
    (`B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set`)
        MINUS (`s 113.1(11.06) — C` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`)

-- (11.05): "if, at October 1 of the year before a three-year period ..., the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the years in that
-- three-year period less the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii) is less than the contribution rate
-- most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) for self-employed persons for those years".
-- src:2925 | Insufficient rates
-- src:2926 | (11.05) Subject to subsections (11.12) and (11.13), if, at October 1 of the year before a three-year period for which a review is required by subsection (1), the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the years in that three-year period less the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii) is less than the contribution rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i) for self-employed persons for those years,
-- out of range: paragraph 45(2)(b) (piece cp3); paragraph 56(2)(c), subsection 58(1.1) and subparagraph 59(c)(ii) (piece cp4). The ratios named in (11.05)(a) are not computed here.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.05) (src:2925-2926)
GIVEN `the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period, at October 1 of the year before` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.05) — the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` `the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period, at October 1 of the year before` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` MEANS
    ((`the rate for self-employed persons for the years in the three-year period, at October 1 of the year before`) MINUS (`the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`))
        LESS THAN (`the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)`)

-- (11.13): "Subsection (11.05) does not apply where (a) a recommendation was made under subsection (1) in the three years before the three year
-- period that the contribution rates ... be increased and the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before that three year period,
-- by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under subsection (6), to give effect to that recommendation; or (b) a recommendation was made
-- ... that the contribution rates ... not be increased and the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before that three year period has
-- caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette."
-- src:2971 | Where subsection (11.05) does not apply
-- src:2972 | (11.13) Subsection (11.05) does not apply where
-- src:2973 | (a) a recommendation was made under subsection (1) in the three years before the three year period referred to in subsection (11.05) that the contribution rates for one or more of the years in that three year period be increased and the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before that three year period, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under subsection (6), to give effect to that recommendation; or
-- src:2974 | (b) a recommendation was made under subsection (1) in the three years before the three year period referred to in subsection (11.05) that the contribution rates for the years in that three year period not be increased and the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before that three year period has caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.13) (src:2971-2974)
GIVEN `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates be increased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates not be increased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.13) — subsection 113.1(11.05) does not apply` `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates be increased` `the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates not be increased` `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette` MEANS
        (`a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates be increased` AND `the rates were increased before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it`)
    OR  (`a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the rates not be increased` AND `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette`)

-- The five cases of subsections (11.07) to (11.11), in the order the text gives them.
-- (11.07) "If neither A nor D is greater than 4.95% and A is greater than D".
-- (11.08) "If A is greater than 4.95%, D is less than or equal to 4.95% and the percentage determined by the formula 1/2(A - D) is less than or
--          equal to 0.1%".   (11.09) the same but "greater than 0.1%".
-- (11.1) "If subsections (11.07) to (11.09) do not apply and the percentage determined by the formula 1/2(A - D) is less than or equal to 0.1%".
-- (11.11) "If subsections (11.07) to (11.1) do not apply".
-- src:2937 | Determination of rate — 1st case
-- src:2938 | (11.07) If neither A nor D is greater than 4.95% and A is greater than D, the contribution rate for employees and employers for each year after the October 1 date referred to in subsection (11.05) is A plus C.
-- src:2939 | Determination of rate — 2nd case
-- src:2940 | (11.08) If A is greater than 4.95%, D is less than or equal to 4.95% and the percentage determined by the formula
-- src:2941 | 1/2(A - D)
-- src:2942 | is less than or equal to 0.1%, then the contribution rate for employees and employers for each year after the October 1 date referred to in subsection (11.05) is the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2943 | 4.95% + 1/2(A - 4.95%) + C
-- src:2944 | Determination of rate — 3rd case
-- src:2945 | (11.09) If A is greater than 4.95%, D is less than or equal to 4.95% and the percentage determined by the formula
-- src:2946 | 1/2(A - D)
-- src:2947 | is greater than 0.1%, then the contribution rate for employees and employers is
-- src:2948 | (a) for the first year after the October 1 date referred to in subsection (11.05), the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2949 | 4.95% + 1/6(A - 4.95%) + C
-- src:2950 | (b) for the next year, the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2951 | 4.95% + 1/3(A - 4.95%) + C
-- src:2952 | and
-- src:2953 | (c) for each subsequent year, the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2954 | 4.95% + 1/2(A - 4.95%) + C
-- src:2955 | Determination of rate — 4th case
-- src:2956 | (11.1) If subsections (11.07) to (11.09) do not apply and the percentage determined by the formula
-- src:2957 | 1/2(A - D)
-- src:2958 | is less than or equal to 0.1%, then the contribution rate for employees and employers for each year after the October 1 date referred to in subsection (11.05) is the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2959 | D + 1/2(A - D) + C
-- src:2960 | Determination of rate — 5th case
-- src:2961 | (11.11) If subsections (11.07) to (11.1) do not apply, then the contribution rate for employees and employers is
-- src:2962 | (a) for the first year after the October 1 date referred to in subsection (11.05), the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2963 | D + 1/6(A - D) + C
-- src:2964 | (b) for the next year, the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2965 | D + 1/3(A - D) + C
-- src:2966 | and
-- src:2967 | (c) for each subsequent year, the rate determined by the formula
-- src:2968 | D + 1/2(A - D) + C
@ref Act s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) (src:2937-2968)
DECLARE `cp6 Case of subsections 113.1(11.07) to (11.11)` IS ONE OF
    `the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)`
    `the second case, subsection 113.1(11.08)`
    `the third case, subsection 113.1(11.09)`
    `the fourth case, subsection 113.1(11.1)`
    `the fifth case, subsection 113.1(11.11)`

@ref Act s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) (src:2937-2968)
GIVEN `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp6 Case of subsections 113.1(11.07) to (11.11)`
`s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` MEANS
    BRANCH IF a AT MOST 4.95% AND d AT MOST 4.95% AND a GREATER THAN d
                THEN `the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)`
           IF a GREATER THAN 4.95% AND d AT MOST 4.95% AND half AT MOST 0.1%
                THEN `the second case, subsection 113.1(11.08)`
           IF a GREATER THAN 4.95% AND d AT MOST 4.95% AND half GREATER THAN 0.1%
                THEN `the third case, subsection 113.1(11.09)`
           IF half AT MOST 0.1%
                THEN `the fourth case, subsection 113.1(11.1)`
           OTHERWISE `the fifth case, subsection 113.1(11.11)`
    WHERE
        a MEANS `s 113.1(11.06) — A` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)`
        d MEANS `s 113.1(11.06) — D` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`
        -- "the percentage determined by the formula 1/2(A - D)"
        half MEANS (a MINUS d) DIVIDED BY 2

-- The rate for the first year after the October 1 date (year 1), the next year (year 2) and each subsequent year (year 3 and later),
-- before the rounding of subsection (11.14). NOTHING: a year number below 1 is not a year after the October 1 date.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) (src:2937-2968)
GIVEN `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` MEANS
    IF `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` LESS THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST rate
    WHERE
        rate MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the case that applies` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set`
            -- (11.07): A plus C, for each year
            WHEN `the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)` THEN a PLUS c
            -- (11.08): 4.95% + 1/2(A - 4.95%) + C, for each year
            WHEN `the second case, subsection 113.1(11.08)` THEN 4.95% PLUS ((a MINUS 4.95%) DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS c
            -- (11.09): 4.95% + 1/6(A - 4.95%) + C, then 1/3, then 1/2
            WHEN `the third case, subsection 113.1(11.09)` THEN 4.95% PLUS ((a MINUS 4.95%) TIMES step) PLUS c
            -- (11.1): D + 1/2(A - D) + C, for each year
            WHEN `the fourth case, subsection 113.1(11.1)` THEN d PLUS ((a MINUS d) DIVIDED BY 2) PLUS c
            -- (11.11): D + 1/6(A - D) + C, then 1/3, then 1/2
            WHEN `the fifth case, subsection 113.1(11.11)` THEN d PLUS ((a MINUS d) TIMES step) PLUS c
        a MEANS `s 113.1(11.06) — A` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)`
        c MEANS `s 113.1(11.06) — C` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`
        d MEANS `s 113.1(11.06) — D` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)`
        -- the fraction of the gap closed: 1/6 in the first year, 1/3 in the next, 1/2 in each subsequent year
        step MEANS
            BRANCH IF `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` EQUALS 1 THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 6
                   IF `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` EQUALS 2 THEN 1 DIVIDED BY 3
                   OTHERWISE 1 DIVIDED BY 2

-- (11.14): "If a contribution rate determined under any of subsections (11.07) to (11.11) is not a multiple of 0.005%, the contribution rate is to be
-- rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%." Halfway rounds up (fork C6-F19).
-- src:2975 | Adjustment
-- src:2976 | (11.14) If a contribution rate determined under any of subsections (11.07) to (11.11) is not a multiple of 0.005%, the contribution rate is to be rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.14) (src:2975-2976)
GIVEN `the rate determined under subsections 113.1(11.07) to (11.11)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` `the rate determined under subsections 113.1(11.07) to (11.11)` MEANS
    (FLOOR (((`the rate determined under subsections 113.1(11.07) to (11.11)`) DIVIDED BY 0.005%) PLUS 0.5)) TIMES 0.005%

@ref Act s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) (src:2937-2976)
GIVEN `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
      `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.07) to (11.14) — the contribution rate for employees and employers for the year, as rounded` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 113.1(11.07) to (11.11) — the contribution rate for employees and employers before rounding` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(i)` `the rate most recently calculated under subparagraph 115(1.1)(c)(ii)` `B, the rate for employees and employers at October 1 of the third year of the last three-year period for which rates were set` `the number of the year after the October 1 date, 1 for the first year`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (`s 113.1(11.14) — the rate rounded to the nearest multiple of 0.005%` rate)

-- (11.05)(b)(ii): "to twice the contribution rate determined under subsections (11.07) to (11.11) for employers for that year".
-- Fork C6-F21: the employers' rate is read as the rate after the rounding of (11.14), so the self-employed rate is twice the rounded rate;
-- the alternative, rounding twice the unrounded rate, differs when the unrounded rate is not a multiple of 0.005% (NOTES.md, fork register).
-- src:2927 | (a) the amount of the benefits payable in respect of the base Canada Pension Plan in the three-year period shall be determined as if the ratios referred to in paragraphs 45(2)(b) and 56(2)(c), subsection 58(1.1) and subparagraph 59(c)(ii) were each 1; and
-- src:2928 | (b) Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended as of the next day after that October 1
-- src:2929 | (i) to increase the contribution rate for employees and employers for each year after that October 1 to the rate determined under subsections (11.07) to (11.11) for that year, and
-- src:2930 | (ii) to increase the contribution rate for self-employed persons for each year after that October 1 to twice the contribution rate determined under subsections (11.07) to (11.11) for employers for that year.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.05)(b)(ii) (src:2927-2930)
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employers for the year, as rounded` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.05)(b)(ii) — the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `the contribution rate for employers for the year, as rounded` MEANS
    (`the contribution rate for employers for the year, as rounded`) TIMES 2

-- (11.05)(b): "Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended as of the next day after that October 1": October 1 of the year before the period.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.05)(b) (src:2927-2930)
GIVEN `the first year of the three-year period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 113.1(11.05)(b) — the day Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` `the first year of the three-year period` MEANS
    YearMonthDay ((`the first year of the three-year period`) MINUS 1) 10 2

-- (11.05) as a whole: the rates are deemed amended when they are insufficient and subsection (11.13) does not take the case out.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.05) (src:2925-2930)
GIVEN `the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 113.1(11.13) takes the case out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.05) — Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended` `the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` `subsection 113.1(11.13) takes the case out` MEANS
    `the rate for self-employed persons is insufficient` AND NOT `subsection 113.1(11.13) takes the case out`

-- (11.05)(a): the benefits are determined "as if the ratios referred to in paragraphs 45(2)(b) and 56(2)(c), subsection 58(1.1) and
-- subparagraph 59(c)(ii) were each 1" -- and (11.12): "Paragraph (11.05)(a) does not apply if subsection (11.07) applies."
-- src:2969 | Where paragraph (11.05)(a) does not apply
-- src:2970 | (11.12) Paragraph (11.05)(a) does not apply if subsection (11.07) applies.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.12) (src:2969-2970)
GIVEN `Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended under subsection 113.1(11.05)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case that applies is the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.05)(a) and (11.12) — the benefits are determined as if the ratios were each 1` `Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended under subsection 113.1(11.05)` `the case that applies is the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)` MEANS
    `Schedule 1 is deemed to have been amended under subsection 113.1(11.05)` AND NOT `the case that applies is the first case, subsection 113.1(11.07)`

§§ `Subsections (11.141) to (11.146) -- the additional Canada Pension Plan`

-- The ranges and the calculations are "set out in the regulations" that subsection (11.144) lets the Governor in Council make; no such regulation
-- is among the texts this encoding reads, so each condition is a yes/no input and the amended rates and portions are NOTHING.
-- src:2977 | Deemed changes to rates — additional Canada Pension Plan
-- src:2978 | (11.141) Subject to subsection (11.143), if, at October 1 of the year before a three-year period for which a review is required by subsection (1), any of the following conditions is met, Schedule 2 is deemed to have been amended as of the next day after that October 1 to change the first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates for each year after that October 1, if required, in accordance with the calculations set out in the regulations:
-- src:2979 | (a) the difference obtained by subtracting the first additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report prepared for the purpose of subsection 115(1) from the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year after that October 1, is within a range set out in the regulations for the purpose of this paragraph;
-- src:2980 | (b) the following differences are within the same range set out in the regulations for the purpose of this paragraph:
-- src:2981 | (i) the difference obtained by subtracting the first additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report prepared for the purpose of subsection 115(1) from the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year after that October 1, and
-- src:2982 | (ii) the difference obtained by subtracting the first additional contribution rate specified in the report prepared for the purpose of section 115 that precedes the report referred to in subparagraph (i), from the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year that is two years before that October 1;
-- src:2983 | (c) the difference obtained by subtracting the second additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report prepared for the purpose of subsection 115(1) from the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year after that October 1, is within a range set out in the regulations for the purpose of this paragraph; or
-- src:2984 | (d) the following differences are within the same range set out in the regulations for the purpose of this paragraph:
-- src:2985 | (i) the difference obtained by subtracting the second additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report prepared for the purpose of subsection 115(1) from the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year after that October 1, and
-- src:2986 | (ii) the difference obtained by subtracting the second additional contribution rate specified in the report prepared for the purpose of section 115 that precedes the report referred to in subparagraph (i), from the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons set out in Schedule 2, for the year that is two years before that October 1.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.141) (src:2977-2986)
GIVEN `the difference in paragraph (a) is within a range set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the differences in paragraph (b) are within the same range set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the difference in paragraph (c) is within a range set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the differences in paragraph (d) are within the same range set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.141) — a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` `the difference in paragraph (a) is within a range set out in the regulations` `the differences in paragraph (b) are within the same range set out in the regulations` `the difference in paragraph (c) is within a range set out in the regulations` `the differences in paragraph (d) are within the same range set out in the regulations` MEANS
        `the difference in paragraph (a) is within a range set out in the regulations`
    OR  `the differences in paragraph (b) are within the same range set out in the regulations`
    OR  `the difference in paragraph (c) is within a range set out in the regulations`
    OR  `the differences in paragraph (d) are within the same range set out in the regulations`

-- The differences of paragraphs (a) and (c): the self-employed rate in Schedule 2 for the year after that October 1 less the rate specified
-- in the most recent report prepared for the purpose of subsection 115(1).
@ref Act s 113.1(11.141)(a), (c) (src:2979, 2983)
GIVEN `the self-employed additional contribution rate set out in Schedule 2 for the year after that October 1` IS A NUMBER
      `the additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.141) — the difference between the Schedule 2 rate and the rate in the most recent report` `the self-employed additional contribution rate set out in Schedule 2 for the year after that October 1` `the additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report` MEANS
    (`the self-employed additional contribution rate set out in Schedule 2 for the year after that October 1`) MINUS (`the additional contribution rate specified in the most recent report`)

-- src:2989 | Non-application of subsections (11.141) and (11.142)
-- src:2990 | (11.143) Subsections (11.141) and (11.142) do not apply if
-- src:2991 | (a) a recommendation was made under subsection (1) in the three years before the three-year period referred to in subsection (11.141) that the first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates for one or more of the years in that three-year period be changed and the rates were changed before October 1 of the year before that three-year period, by an Act of Parliament or by a regulation made under subsection (6), to give effect to that recommendation; or
-- src:2992 | (b) a recommendation was made under subsection (1) in the three years before the three-year period referred to in subsection (11.141) that the first additional contribution rates or second additional contribution rates for the years in that three-year period not be changed and the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before that three-year period has caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.143) (src:2989-2992)
GIVEN `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates be changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rates were changed before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates not be changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.143) — subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates be changed` `the rates were changed before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it` `a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates not be changed` `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette` MEANS
        (`a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates be changed` AND `the rates were changed before October 1 of the year before the period to give effect to it`)
    OR  (`a recommendation was made in the three years before the period that the first or second additional rates not be changed` AND `the Minister of Finance before October 1 of the year before the period caused that recommendation to be published in the Canada Gazette`)

@ref Act s 113.1(11.141) (src:2977-2986)
GIVEN `a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113.1(11.141) — Schedule 2 is deemed to have been amended` `a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` `subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply` MEANS
    `a condition for the deemed change to the additional contribution rates is met` AND NOT `subsections 113.1(11.141) and (11.142) do not apply`

-- Not covered: the calculations are in regulations that are not deposited.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.141) (src:2977-2986)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 113.1(11.141) — the first or second additional contribution rate for a year after a deemed amendment` year MEANS
    NOTHING

-- src:2987 | Determination of benefits — additional Canada Pension Plan
-- src:2988 | (11.142) Subject to subsection (11.143), if, at October 1 of the year before a three-year period for which a review is required by subsection (1), any of the conditions set out in paragraphs (11.141)(a) to (d) is met, the portions of benefits under this Act in respect of the additional Canada Pension Plan, for each year after that October 1, shall be determined in accordance with the regulations.
@ref Act s 113.1(11.142) (src:2987-2988)
